For Egyptian filmmaker Sara Shazli , the camera became a way of asking her mother questions she had carried since childhood. Returning to Cairo from film school in Cuba, she would wait in the family kitchen, camera in hand, hoping to understand the woman whose devotion to cinema had so often left her feeling alone.

&#x201C;Was the camera protecting me from the answers she could give me? Was the camera a way of having her attention?,&#x201D; Shazli wonders. With cinema occupying such a central place in her mother&#x2019;s life, filming their conversations offered a way of reaching her through the very medium that had so often kept them apart. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories How Soviet TV Audiences Fell Under the Spell of Mass Hypnosis Artist Anatoly Kashpirovskiy Ji.hlava New Visions Award Winner Karim Akalay Mixes Magic With ‘Anti-Social Realism’ in ‘6TM’: ‘It’s About Collective Strength Rather Than One Hero’

Those encounters became the foundation of &#x201C; Your Daughter ,&#x201D; Shazli&#x2019;s documentary about her relationship with her mother Marianne Khoury , the Egyptian producer and filmmaker who spent decades working alongside her uncle, renowned director Youssef Chahine. Premiering at the 47th Cairo Intl. Film Festival, the film charts a daughter&#x2019;s changing understanding of her mother, from resentment over her childhood absence to an admiration she had never anticipated.

Shazli initially conceived the project as a search for Woody, the nanny who had helped raise her, hoping to reconnect with a figure who had played such an important role in her childhood. But as she developed the film and attended workshops with other filmmakers, their observations helped her recognize a more deeply personal story taking shape in the footage of her mother.

&#x201C;Someone told me, &#x2018;Look at how you film your mother. You film her with so much love,&#x2019;&#x201D; she recalls. &#x201C;It was actually painful,&#x201D; she adds, because acknowledging that love meant confronting difficult questions, ones she had avoided for far too long. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Those questions extended beyond Khoury&#x2019;s absence to the expectations she passed on to her daughter. &#x201C;I grew up with a mother telling me that you have to be independent from any man in the world,&#x201D; Shazli says. &#x201C;But it was so extreme. Why can&#x2019;t both the dad and the mom help? Why can&#x2019;t both be responsible?&#x201D;

Khoury had built her career while shouldering much of the financial burden and everyday demands of family life. Shazli admired her mother&#x2019;s determination but questioned the sacrifices that came along with it. She sought a different kind of partnership, with a husband who shares childcare and financial responsibilities, rather than carrying those burdens alone.

Her family&#x2019;s cinematic legacy brought pressures of its own. Growing up around Chahine, whom she affectionately calls &#x201C;Uncle Joe,&#x201D; Shazli struggled to establish her own identity as a filmmaker.

&#x201C;Nobody put that pressure on me,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;It was me, coming from that Chahine family, being compared to such a titan. What are you going to do with all this?&#x201D; Studying film in Cuba offered distance from her family and from Egypt, helping her discover what she wanted to say as a filmmaker.

&#x201C;I started to see her differently and I started to feel for her,&#x201D; Shazli tells Variety of her conversations with Khoury. She came to understand how her mother&#x2019;s own upbringing had shaped the way she expressed affection. &#x201C;It did hurt me to realize that she had grown up with a different kind of love, one where affection wasn&#x2019;t always expressed through time and attention. She gave what she knew. You give what you receive.&#x201D;

Her growing empathy did not erase the hurt of her childhood, but it allowed her to see Khoury beyond the role of mother. Khoury, who took over Chahine&#x2019;s production outfit Misr International after his passing, remains as devoted to her work as ever, but Shazli no longer sees that devotion solely through the lens of what she missed growing up.

Becoming a mother herself brought another shift in perspective. &#x201C;Now I feel like I really admire her,&#x201D; Shazli says. &#x201C;How on earth did she manage to do all this?&#x201D;

&#x201C;That says a lot about her energy, about how much ambition she has,&#x201D; she adds. &#x201C;I&#x2019;m nowhere near that, and I&#x2019;m alright with that too. I&#x2019;m actually happy that I don&#x2019;t have that because you suffer when you have that. You want to be everywhere and do everything.&#x201D; But that admiration does not mean she intends to follow the same path. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

For Shazli, whose earlier documentary &#x201C;Back Home&#x201D; explored her relationship with her father, filmmaking is also a means of working through deeply personal questions. &#x201C;For me, filmmaking is really about healing,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;If there&#x2019;s no problem, there&#x2019;s no film. If there&#x2019;s nothing to discover, to heal, to dig deep into, there&#x2019;s no film.&#x201D;

The Cairo premiere has brought an unexpected response, including from men who recognized their own family relationships in the film. &#x201C;When somebody comes and tells you, &#x2018;You made me want to speak to my mother,&#x2019; or &#x2018;You made me want to speak to my father,&#x2019; that&#x2019;s exactly what it should do,&#x201D; she says.

But having explored both parents on screen, Shazli is ready to turn toward fiction. &#x201C;I did a film about my dad. I did a film about my mom. I&#x2019;m done,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;Now I want to have more fun. I want to write a fiction. I want to work with actors. I want to create differently now.&#x201D;

Steven Paul , a special advisor to President Donald Trump who has lobbied for a U.S. federal tax credit alongside special ambassador to Hollywood Jon Voight , said he hopes the incentive will be &#x201C;active&#x201D; in some form by January 2027.

Speaking at the Doha Industry Days &#x2013; the industry component of the Doha Film Festival &#x2013; during a fireside chat moderated by Variety &#x2019;s Nick Vivarelli, Paul said &#x201C;we still have a little ways to go&#x201D; in terms of making the proposed tax credit a reality. &#x201C;There&#x2019;s a bill that&#x2019;s written, and already we put together a very big coalition of almost everybody representing the entertainment business,&#x201D; he added, mentioning he has the support of members from organizations such as SAG, DGA, and the Writers Guild of America. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Hollywood Has Flipped on GenAI, Says 'Avatar' VFX House Weta FX Chief: 'If You Don’t Have an AI Strategy, Don’t Bother'

&#x201C;What has to happen is it has to be attached to some sort of a bill,&#x201D; he continued. &#x201C;This is stuff that I've never been involved in. This is now the politics of it all, where they all now go into sessions and negotiate with each other and all of that. So we're hoping that it gets attached to a bill, whatever that bill will be now, in the upcoming weeks and gets voted on before the end of the year so that it would actually be active starting in January.&#x201D;

Paul serves as chairman, founder, and CEO of Crystal Sky Pictures and SP Media Group. He has shepherded several box-office successes in years past, including the Baby Geniuses franchise, &#x201C;Ghost Rider&#x201D; and &#x201C;Ghost Rider 2: Spirit of Vengeance&#x201D; starring Nicolas Cage, &#x201C;Ghost in the Shell&#x201D; starring Scarlett Johansson, and the Lionsgate-distributed &#x201C;Rambo: Last Blood.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The producer recalled telling Trump he was &#x201C;ashamed&#x201D; to be shooting his next film about the early years of Richard Nixon in England. The president, in response, said that wasn&#x2019;t &#x201C;right.&#x201D; It was at that meeting that Paul convinced the president of the need for a federal tax credit. &#x201C;Finally, he supported it, and we now have a tremendous energy behind it.&#x201D;

Asked about the intricacies of the proposed rebate, Paul said it is &#x201C;between 20 and 30% government federal tax credit.&#x201D; The benefit starts at a base of 20%, and then there are two uplifts: if you&#x2019;re an independent production, you get an extra 5%; and if you are filming in an area &#x201C;considered a disaster zone,&#x201D; you get another 5%. Given the recent devastating fires, California now qualifies as a disaster zone, the producer noted.

&#x201C;That goes on top of a state tax credit,&#x201D; he emphasized. &#x201C;So you can go into Jersey, you can go into New York, you can go anywhere, and it goes right on top of it. That means you get both of them. You can get the 20 or 30% state tax credit and potentially up to another 20 to 30% on the federal.&#x201D;

Would a combined tax credit of up to 50 or 60% cause states to possibly reduce their local breaks? Paul &#x201C;doesn&#x2019;t believe&#x201D; so. &#x201C;I think they'll still all want to outbid each other, so they might even increase it. I don't think anybody's gonna reduce their tax credits in the state. That's my guess.&#x201D;

The producer sees the federal tax credit as essential to bring productions back to the U.S., but mentioned how, even with a combined 50-60% credit, the country might still struggle to lure major productions away from European hubs like Hungary and Romania because of the high production costs in the U.S.. &#x201C;It is still probably advantageous to shoot in these other places.&#x201D;

When asked what he believes was the catalyst for the big Hollywood exodus, Paul responded with the 2023 Writers Guild of America strike. &#x201C;We [ended] up not having production for a while, and then people [went] off and [to] find other ways to make production.&#x201D;

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s almost the same way unscripted got started because there was a writers&#x2019; strike at that time period,&#x201D; he said, referring to the 2007-2008 strike. &#x201C;I hate these strikes. I think it's always counterproductive. I think people should just never strike, get into a room, negotiate hard, just get something done because those strikes end up hurting everybody. You always have a failed win, and I think that was one of them.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Paul reiterated he has the support of all major Hollywood studios, including the newly-formed Skydance. &#x201C;We&#x2019;ve been making films with Paramount for the past eight years, and we have a relationship with David Ellison,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;Even though it was competitive at one moment, we now like each other. I think it&#x2019;s going to be healthy. I think there'll be a lot more production that takes place. David is a filmmaker. He really cares about the entertainment business, and I think that's gonna be good. I'm optimistic about that.&#x201D;

The producer said the execs &#x201C;love the idea of bringing a certain amount of productions back to America.&#x201D; &#x201C;Our stages are empty. They all have studios. Paramount has a lot of sound stages. Everybody has sound stages, and we want them full.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I've met with almost every head of every major studio, who are all championing it,&#x201D; he continued. They themselves are getting on the phones to call people, congresspeople, to help make it happen because they know how important it is for them [to hit] their bottom line.&#x201D;

Paul is &#x201C;thankful&#x201D; for Trump&#x2019;s seemingly dismissal of his previously fervent support of a 100% tariff on films produced outside of the U.S. as a way of countering foreign tax incentives. &#x201C;Thankfully, I haven't heard the word tariff. In the beginning, we were hearing tariffs all the time. That was the thing. When I came here last time, it was the tariff, but no. Now it's all hands on deck, federal tax credit.&#x201D;

Corporate affairs director of the U.K.&#x2019;s famed Pinewood Studios , Andrew M. Smith, said he cannot yet confirm whether or not the next Bond film will be shot on their lot, but that he and his team are keeping their &#x201C;fingers crossed.&#x201D;

Speaking at a panel about locations at the Doha Industry Days moderated by Variety&#x2019; s Nick Vivarelli, Smith said he &#x201C;wishes&#x201D; he could talk about whether or not the franchise will return to Pinewood, but it&#x2019;s still early days. &#x201C;I&#x2019;m thrilled that Bond&#x2019;s been announced,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;We&#x2019;re talking about it. We&#x2019;re the home of Bond. Fingers crossed.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories The Game Awards Adds Disney+ to Livestream Lineup Disney+ and ‘The House of Flowers’ Director Manolo Caro Prep Series Adaptation of ‘Blood Wedding’ by Federico García Lorca (EXCLUSIVE)

Five days ago, the film world came to a brief halt when Robert Pattinson was announced as the new 007 following months of speculation on who would take on the sacred tuxedo from Daniel Craig. Craig&#x2019;s five-movie run as the womanizing super spy began in 2006 with &#x201C;Casino Royale&#x201D; and ended with 2021&#x2019;s &#x201C;No Time to Die,&#x201D; which ends with Bond sacrificing himself to save the world from a secret global terrorist organization.

&#x201C;No Time to Die&#x201D; was also the last film in the series released before longtime producers Michael G. Wilson and Barbara Broccoli sold creative control of the franchise to Amazon MGM for $20 million. Pinewood competitor Shepperton Studios has traditionally been the home of Amazon in the U.K., but it seems Bond&#x2019;s long-standing tradition with Pinewood might lure the high-profile production to its lot.

Amazon MGM Studios has a long-term partnership with Pinewood Group in the U.K. and Canada. Back in October, the U.S. studio secured a multi-million-dollar deal at Pinewood Toronto. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Elsewhere in the conversation, Smith also spoke about attracting major U.S. productions to the U.K. thanks to a combination of healthy tax rebates, top infrastructure and highly-skilled crews. &#x201C;You've got to have good infrastructure, you've got to have a good skill base, and you've got to have good incentives. But I think the incentive is probably [the bigger attraction].&#x201D;

&#x201C;I mean, we heard yesterday from Steven Paul that his film about President Nixon is being filmed in the U.K. Is Pinewood better than Paramount? No. It&#x2019;s the money,&#x201D; he added, noting how he doesn&#x2019;t believe American productions are flocking to the U.K. because of any key differences in either infrastructure or crews.

The veteran believes, however, that they have been &#x201C;very fortunate&#x201D; in their positioning in the U.K., particularly when it comes to keeping 59 of their 61 stages under lease by major American studios like Disney and Netflix. Out of 38 Marvel films, for example, 21 have been shot at Pinewood.

&#x201C;Would you invest in any more stages in mature markets? I don't think you would at the moment. I think what we're trying to do is innovate for the future,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;In new markets you need to think very carefully about building new stages. There&#x2019;s a lot of empty stages in the world right now, especially in mature markets.&#x201D;

For now, Pinewood is keeping its eye on Bond, but also branching out to new technology, content creation and short-form. The studios recently struck a partnership with the U.K. government for the CoSTAR Network, a &#xA3;75.6 million investment by the UKRI Infrastructure Fund and delivered by the Arts and Humanities Research Council (AHRC). Based at Pinewood Studios, it is a national hub for creative businesses to &#x201C;test and take new ideas to market […] strengthening the U.K.&#x2019;s standing as a world leader in creative technology,&#x201D; according to a Pinewood statement.

At the panel, Smith emphasized the importance of embracing technology and new formats, noting how content creators working on moving into long-form content might be &#x201C;the next Russo Brothers.&#x201D;

